# Build the delivery-volume meter

From [Decide the Telegram delivery bar](./decide-telegram-delivery-bar.svx):
judgment drifts loose silently — the fix must police itself instead of rotting
like the prose rules did.

Resolved when:

- A scheduled check (Inngest, `packages/system-bus`) counts the last 24h of
  `delivery.requested` + `fallback.delivered` off the Convex stream.
- Over ~24/day (2× the ~12 target) it sends exactly one notify with the count
  and top sources — evidence, once, not a repeating alarm; a cap/latch keeps
  it from becoming the next spam source.
- The threshold and target live as named constants with the settlement's date
  and reasoning next to them.
- Tests cover the count, the single-fire latch, and the quiet path.

## Result (2026-07-29)

Delivered by pi worker (pane w28:p0), reviewed and committed by steering.
`packages/system-bus/src/inngest/functions/delivery-volume-meter.ts` + test:
daily 08:00 America/Los_Angeles cron pages the count of `delivery.requested` +
`fallback.delivered` over the last 24h with the top three producers when it
reaches `PAGE_THRESHOLD = 24`; a Redis NX latch
(`joelclaw:delivery-volume-meter:paged`) guarantees single-fire, released only
after a full window at or under `TARGET_DELIVERIES_PER_DAY = 12` (and released
immediately if the page itself fails to send). Notify uses a stable
content-hashed eventId so Inngest retries cannot double-page. Host-registered
only (needs local Convex + `joelclaw` CLI); 5 tests pass. Deploy = restart the
host worker so Inngest re-registers the function.
